WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.590
Three pages on an exam desk.

2
00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:04.390
One in short lines.

3
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:07.850
One with names in capitals
and lines in brackets.

4
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:10.090
One in full paragraphs.

5
00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:13.120
A magnifying glass slides over each one.

6
00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:16.320
On every page, a
different patch lights up.

7
00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:17.400
Same exam.

8
00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.890
Same question.

9
00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:22.090
So does the form change what you look for?

10
00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:26.010
In this mission, you'll meet
the four forms Paper 1 can set:

11
00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:30.520
prose fiction, prose
non-fiction, poetry and drama.

12
00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:34.900
You'll test whether one set of
questions really works on every page.

13
00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:39.630
And you'll open a Wilde comedy,
and ask what its brackets are for.

14
00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:43.740
Your mission: decide whether
form changes what you look for.
